// Title: HackTool - Kerbrute Execution - Linux
// Sigma ID: e839522a-d2dc-4e8d-89e1-0d7b1a3c6b50
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2026-04-21 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: reconnaissance, credential-access, discovery, T1087.002, T1110.003
// Description: Detects execution of Kerbrute, a tool for brute-forcing and enumerating valid Active Directory
//   accounts through Kerberos pre-authentication. Commonly used for domain user enumeration,
//   password spraying, and AS-REP roasting target discovery.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://github.com/ropnop/kerbrute
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/6b9ade7935a13d35a57e75ff2587fbedcc53ef56/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_hktl_kerbrute.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath contains "/kerbrute" or (ProcessCommandLine contains " userenum " or ProcessCommandLine contains " bruteuser " or ProcessCommandLine contains " passwordspray " or ProcessCommandLine contains " bruteforce ")
